.TH ACC-AGENT 1 2026-10-22 "ACC" "ACC Manual"
.SH NAME
acc-agent \- run one ACC agent (a cell) on the collective's bus
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B acc-agent
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B acc-agent
is the process behind every agent in an ACC collective.
One process is one cell: it loads its configuration, builds its backends
(bus, vector store, working memory, LLM), connects to NATS, loads its role
definition, and announces itself.
It then runs its loops concurrently \(em heartbeat, task processing, role
updates \(em until it receives SIGINT or SIGTERM, when it drains and closes
its connections.
.PP
The command takes no arguments: everything comes from the configuration
file and the environment.
It is normally started by the stack
.RB ( acc-deploy (1),
the operator on Kubernetes), one container per role, not by hand.
.PP
A role's governance travels with the role definition: the constitutional
rules, the setpoints and learned rules, the category ceiling, and the
oversight queue the agent must route risky actions through.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Any key of \fIacc\-config.yaml\fR can be overridden; these are the ones a
deployment usually sets.
.TP
.B ACC_CONFIG_PATH
The configuration file (default: found through the layout in
.BR acc (1)).
.TP
.B ACC_AGENT_ROLE
The role this cell takes.
.TP
.B ACC_COLLECTIVE_ID
The collective the cell joins.
.TP
.B ACC_NATS_URL
The bus.
.TP
.B ACC_DEPLOY_MODE
\fBstandalone\fR, \fBrhoai\fR or \fBedge\fR: where the cell runs, which
decides where roles are loaded from and which signing defaults apply.
.TP
.B ACC_OPERATOR_MODE
The security floor; \fBdev\fR tolerates absent secrets and lowers the
signing and authentication floors for local use.
.TP
.BR ACC_LLM_BACKEND ", " ACC_LLM_MODEL ", " ACC_LLM_BASE_URL
The LLM backend (for example \fBollama\fR, \fBanthropic\fR, \fBvllm\fR,
\fBopenai_compat\fR), the model and the endpoint.
.TP
.B ACC_LLM_API_KEY_ENV
The \fIname\fR of the variable that holds the API key; the key itself is
never put in the configuration.
.TP
.BR ACC_VECTOR_BACKEND ", " ACC_LANCEDB_PATH ", " ACC_MILVUS_URI
The vector store: \fBlancedb\fR, \fBmilvus\fR or \fBturbovec\fR.
.TP
.B ACC_REDIS_URL
Working memory.
.TP
.B ACC_SIGNING_MODE
How role updates are signed: \fBed25519\fR, \fBspiffe\fR or \fBauto\fR.
.TP
.B ACC_ROLES_ROOT
The roles tree.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.BR SIGINT ", " SIGTERM
Stop taking work, drain, close the bus connection and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I acc\-config.yaml
The cell's configuration; see the layout in
.BR acc (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR acc (1),
.BR acc-cli (1),
.BR acc-deploy (1)
